# swarm-os — env for `examples/docker-compose.dist.yml`.
#
# This is the file `docker-compose.dist.yml` refers to. It is the same content
# as the repo-root `.env.example` (which `install.sh` copies); keep them in
# sync if you edit one. Two ways to use it:
#
#     cp examples/.env.example .env && ./install.sh
#     # or, manually, from the directory that holds the .env:
#     set -a && source .env && set +a
#     docker compose -f examples/docker-compose.dist.yml up -d
#
# Read with `source`, so values may use ${HOME}. One KEY=VALUE per line, no
# spaces around `=`, no inline comments.

# ── Image — SET IT EXPLICITLY ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The compose file writes `image: ${SWARM_OS_IMAGE:-ghcr.io/luminis1986/swarm-os:latest}`,
# so an UNSET variable still starts a container — silently, off the fallback.
# Do not rely on that fallback:
#   * the container reports its own image from this variable, so unset means
#     the UI cannot say what it is running;
#   * one-click self-update refuses on sight (`IMAGE TAG IS HARDCODED`,
#     status `image_not_interpolated`) because SWARM_OS_IMAGE is what an update
#     REWRITES in this file — swarm-os edits this exact line, in place, leaving
#     a `.bak` beside it. A variable that is not here is a variable it will not
#     rewrite;
#   * a single-segment value (`swarm-os:latest`) is a locally-built image with
#     nothing behind it to pull → `image_not_registry`, also refused.
# Pulling from the private package needs a prior `docker login ghcr.io` with a
# PAT that has `read:packages` (see docs/deploy/install.en.md).
SWARM_OS_IMAGE=ghcr.io/luminis1986/swarm-os:latest

# ── Update detection (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# GitHub PAT used to READ the releases of luminis1986/swarm-os. The repository
# is private, so an unauthenticated call answers 404: without this token the
# check status stays `no_token` and no new version is ever announced. It is
# never used to write anything, and never leaves the container except as an
# Authorization header to api.github.com.
#   * classic PAT → scope `repo` (read access to a private repo);
#   * fine-grained PAT → the swarm-os repository, permission `Contents: Read`.
#   * NOT the same thing as the `read:packages` PAT used by `docker login` —
#     that one cannot read releases. One may hold both scopes; swarm-os only
#     ever reads this variable.
# Empty is a healthy state: it means "never tell me about releases".
# It only reaches the container because `docker-compose.dist.yml` names it in
# its `environment:` allow-list — a variable that is not named there is invisible
# to the process however it is defined here.
SWARM_OS_GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ── Identity ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shown in the UI, logs and Discord notifications. One instance == one project.
SWARM_OS_PROJECT_NAME=my-project
# Docker container name. Must be unique per instance on the host.
SWARM_OS_CONTAINER_NAME=swarm-os

# ── Host paths — EDIT THESE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The project the agents work in (read-write).
WORKSPACE_PATH=${HOME}/dev/my-project
# Persistent state: SQLite DB, auth tokens, logs/, backups/, .claude-runtime/.
DATA_PATH=${HOME}/.swarm-os/my-project
# Your authenticated Claude Code dir, mounted READ-ONLY. REQUIRED.
# You must have run the Claude Code CLI and logged in at least once so that
# ${CLAUDE_DIR}/.credentials.json exists — agents cannot start otherwise.
CLAUDE_DIR=${HOME}/.claude
# Claude theme/auth file (read-only). Prevents the first-spawn theme picker
# from freezing a session. Leave as-is on a standard install.
CLAUDE_JSON=${HOME}/.claude.json

# ── Ports (host loopback only — NEVER bind 0.0.0.0) ───────────────────────────
# Host-side port for the web UI. The container always listens on 8787 inside.
SWARM_OS_PORT=8787
# VS Code web editor port. Host port must equal the container port (1:1).
SWARM_OS_IDE_PORT=8790

# ── Remote access / notifications (optional) ──────────────────────────────────
# Base URL the operator reaches the UI at — used for Discord deep-links only
# (no token is ever included). e.g. https://my-host.tailnet.ts.net:8787
SWARM_OS_PUBLIC_URL=
# Discord webhook for idle / orchestrator-ended notifications. Empty = disabled.
SWARM_OS_DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=

# ── Agent providers — multi-provider (optional) ───────────────────────────────
# Agents can run on four CLIs: `claude` (Anthropic), `codex` (OpenAI), `gemini`
# (Google) and `opencode` (models via OpenRouter), picked per team AND per
# agent. Full guide: docs/providers.md.
#
# Two host facts decide whether the non-claude ones are usable at all:
#   * the image ships ONLY the claude CLI, so under the default `local`
#     transport (what this compose file sets up) the other three report
#     themselves unavailable — correct behaviour, not a misconfiguration;
#   * under the `ssh` transport the agent runs on the HOST with the host's own
#     credentials, so each CLI must be installed AND logged in there
#     (`codex login`, `gemini`, `claude`). swarm-os ships no API key.
# A CLI installed on the host becomes selectable at the next availability poll
# (60 s) — no container restart.
#
# As with SWARM_OS_GITHUB_TOKEN, any variable below only reaches the container
# if the compose service names it in its `environment:` allow-list.

# Provider used when neither the request nor the role names one. Built-in ids
# only: claude|codex|gemini|opencode. Validated at boot — an unknown value
# stops the server instead of silently falling back.
# SWARM_OS_DEFAULT_PROVIDER=claude

# Host-side state directory of each CLI, where the per-session credential
# symlinks point (siblings of SWARM_OS_HOST_CLAUDE_DIR, `ssh` transport only).
# WARNING: the default derives from the CONTAINER's home (/home/node/.codex and
# friends), a path that does not exist on the host. Left unset under `ssh` the
# symlinks dangle, the agent starts with no visible error, and its first turn
# fails on an authentication error.
# SWARM_OS_HOST_CODEX_DIR=${HOME}/.codex
# SWARM_OS_HOST_GEMINI_DIR=${HOME}/.gemini
# SWARM_OS_HOST_OPENCODE_DIR=${HOME}/.opencode

# Authentication method a gemini agent pins (`security.auth.selectedType`):
# oauth-personal | gemini-api-key | vertex-ai | compute-default-credentials.
# Under `ssh` the container cannot see the host's ~/.gemini, so it cannot tell
# whether the OAuth credentials are there; it defaults to `gemini-api-key`,
# whose failure at least shows up in the PTY. If the host is logged in with a
# Google account, say so here — an unpinned value opens gemini's auth picker,
# a modal that repaints for ever and makes the agent look permanently busy.
# SWARM_OS_GEMINI_AUTH_TYPE=oauth-personal

# OpenRouter API key used by `opencode` agents — its only credential mechanism
# (there is no `opencode login`). THE MAIN PATH IS THE UI: SETTINGS ▸ OPENROUTER
# stores it server-side, masks it on read, and applies it to the next agent
# spawn with no restart. This variable is only a dev/CI fallback: it is used
# when NO key is stored, and a stored key always wins over it. With neither,
# opencode reads as unavailable ("installed but no OpenRouter API key").
# SWARM_OS_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# ── Optional overrides (defaults applied by docker-compose.dist.yml) ──────────
# SWARM_OS_DEFAULT_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8   # unset = the default model of SWARM_OS_DEFAULT_PROVIDER
# SWARM_OS_DEFAULT_EFFORT=xhigh          # low|medium|high|xhigh|max (xhigh is costly)
# SWARM_OS_MAX_ORCHESTRATORS=10
# SWARM_OS_MAX_WORKERS_PER_ORCH=20
# SWARM_OS_LOG_LEVEL=info                # trace|debug|info|warn|error|fatal
# SWARM_OS_IDE_ENABLED=true              # false disables the VS Code web editor
